  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening vaccination services for mobile and hard-to-reach populations along the mobility continuum in Guinea (RSS3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Guinea, in collaboration with national authorities, local communities and partners including Gavi, WHO and UNICEF, work to strengthen equitable access to vaccination and other essential health services for mobile and hard-to-reach populations, particularly in border areas and locations with high levels of population mobility. Activities are implemented at priority points of entry and in strategic health districts to improve vaccination coverage, strengthen epidemiological surveillance, enhance cross-border coordination and support the management of epidemic risks. Through these interventions, the project contributes to health security and inclusive access to healthcare for communities that may be underserved by traditional health services.</narrative>
  </description>
